  "scope": "Scheduled, terminal and replay retry journal policy over unchanged native request admission, bounded codecs, dispatch-history decoding, storage writes, group finalization and consuming immediate transactions.",
  "limitations": [
    "Frozen policy shares native request admission, codecs, storage, lease validation and group finalization primitives, not the migrated retry orchestration.",
    "Disposable corrupt SQLite fixtures restore constraints before the production call. They are not valid recovery checkpoints or new lease authority.",
    "Internal memory retry keeps lease-before-proposal admission and partial mutation on terminal finalization failure. Public retry entry retains its separate terminal replay and authority policy.",
    "Durable replay preserves original terminal admission, not new result/request correspondence. Unknown non-completed raw states retain their original branch, not new recovery admission.",
    "Direct hooks model quota/codec errors and uncertain commits/unwinds. Real SQLite triggers and deferred constraints cover scheduled and terminal write/commit rollback; no physical disk-full or power-loss experiment is claimed.",
    "No new Linux, remote CI, live GUI, standalone exported-source execution, complete host-neutral durable recovery or throughput benchmark is claimed."
  ],
